      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright (c) 2010 Elsevier Masson SAS. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "A series of 2-methylaminobenzimidazole derivatives (1-11) were synthesized by the reaction of 2-(chloromethyl)-1H-benzimidazole derivatives with primary aromatic amines. All these compounds were characterized by IR, 1H NMR, 13C NMR, GC-MS and elemental analysis. The newly synthesized compounds were screened for analgesic and anti-inflammatory activities on acetic acid induced writhing in mice and carrageenan induced paw oedema in rats. Compounds (7) and (2) showed a potent analgesic (89% at 100 mg/kg b.w) and anti-inflammatory (100% at 100 mg/kg b.w) activities compared with standard drug Nimesulide (100% at 50 mg/kg b.w) respectively. The other compounds showed good analgesic and anti-inflammatory activities."
      },
